{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: the bounded archive capacity capture build, with the BR-4 deadline partial.\n\nHead 102169dd08a3a6f3b6228de24f9085c8369e75dd, tree d89994d0, branch request/archive-capacity-20261026. Main 994a638f is the merge base (merge d6204988 carries the approved K1 page). The delta is 12 paths, 1,092 insertions and 16 deletions. Review request bb077aad (it replaces 05ff3c74), checker promise 5c022e8b, child request 7e4b543c (builder promise fe7fca47), parent 0f0eeab7, BR-4 partial under 15b0f8ab, planner rulings 6634c94c and b8a6c843, planner answer eb0cc06e. Primary artifact 308fc21e (the PD-2 note), first of 16 at this head. All 16 rest on promise fe7fca47 and request 7e4b543c only. They replace the first filing (414d507a and its siblings), which rested on BR-4 15b0f8ab and which gs refused as a broken reporting link (my assert 602e0229). No source, note or evidence changed.\n\nRead order: the note in full; 7e4b543c, b8a6c843 and my question dfad64c7; every production path (archive-capacity-observation.ts in full, the archive-driver, archive-finish-cost and archive-adaptive hunks); the witness tests; the paired-control probe and its result; the final gate record; the manifest and the sealed directory. I did not run any suite again.\n\nCapture (7e4b543c):\n1. Default only. The driver observes only when it builds the default production budget itself (\"production\" in options and no supplied factory). A supplied factory is called once, and its budget is registered as unobserved: no ledger read, row, quote, selection or terminal geometry is kept for it.\n2. Debits unchanged. ObservedArchiveBudget subclasses ArchiveBudget and calls super.spend and super.canSpend once each, with the same cost object. A canSpend inside spend is not recorded twice (depth guard). Every observer step runs inside safely(), so an observer error sets a flag and cannot replace the archive result or exception. forecastArchiveFinish returns the same sum as before, and the quote object it passes reads only values that the original code had already computed. The planner-side capture in archive-adaptive adds two calls with no debit.\n3. Target identity. captureThroughHash comes from the native heads (row.pending.through, the conversion through, or selectedThrough). The Native fixed-next witness checks firstQuote.throughHash and selectedQuote.throughHash against the confirmed receipt.\n4. First finish against terminal. firstFinishAttribution is frozen at the first completed quote (stage 0), and later writer work cannot change it. The terminal record keeps its own flags. In the witness, first-finish attribution is complete, the terminal site table overflows, and the terminal is reported as incomplete.\n5. Incomplete flags. Unknown sites, the site and refusal caps, malformed input, counter overflow, observer errors, ledger mismatch and custom budgets each set a named flag. observationComplete also requires the row context, a complete first quote whose components sum to its total, a target hash and a terminal record.\n6. Privacy. The observer copies only own data properties named in closed lists, natural numbers, booleans, one validated digest, fixed labels, and frames as (code, line, column) from a fixed table of public source paths. The Native witness walks every leaf of the real capture: each must be a safe natural number, a boolean, null, a sha256 throughHash, or one of the two fixed labels. It also checks that the token and repository values are absent, and that the same predicate rejects one added byte of content.\n7. Completeness witness (Native, fixed-next): the captured first-quote total equals fixedFinish.remaining; the first-quote ledger and the first-finish attribution equal fixedFinish.used; the final ledger equals the existing diagnostic cost; ledgerReconciled is true.\n\nPaired controls (raw result read). The three compiled controls run the real bundled observer and ArchiveBudget in local workerd, on a retained numeric fixture with one synthetic aggregate debit:\n- Omitting the frontier component makes the geometry assertion fail.\n- One byte of content makes the privacy assertion fail.\n- A compiled build that forwards one changed metadata unit makes the original-ledger assertion fail.\nThe note labels them correctly: they replay numbers, not the Native plan, SQL or authority. The completeness and privacy controls change the observer's input or output rather than a production call site, so they show that the assertions discriminate. That is what 7e4b543c asked for. The Native witness carries the real-path checks.\n\nBR-4 partial (15b0f8ab):\n- local-archive-command.ts:78: the kill timer for each concurrent replay child goes from 30,000 to 90,000 ms.\n- archive-installed.test.ts:1607: the Grow production follower case goes from 30,000 to 100,000 ms.\n- The sample is the two complete follower observations, 25,668 and 29,457 ms: median 27,562.5 ms, three times that 82,687.5 ms. The 30,084 ms run is censored and is not used.\n- The Native producer, the clone, and every production budget and clock stay at 30,000 ms. The 8 MiB output bound, authentication, report and secret checks, and every assertion are unchanged.\n- The failing run at a5a29091 was this inner timer (30,078 ms, \"local clone fixture refused\"). The note labels that diagnosis as source-based.\n- The follower passed at 29,668 ms in the final gate. The note says BR-4 stays open; this landing retires nothing of BR-4.\n- docs/testing.md lines 338-344 add the harness rule. The planner adopted that rule in this head (eb0cc06e item 2). It names the offline public archive command and states that it does not raise a Native producer or protocol deadline. It sits in \"Time, size and setup\" beside the scope project's allowance, and the reason is repeated in both test comments. The head files the docs directory artifact (adc81cf9) as well as docs/testing.md, as eb0cc06e requires. Planner answer eb0cc06e accepts both values, 90,000 ms per child and 100,000 ms for the follower, as the one BR-4 repair.\n\nValidation:\n- Earlier gates stay recorded as failures or interruptions: a722070f (stale seal), fe211cd0 (interrupted), a5a29091 (sole follower failure; 794 Native passed, 1 failed, 2 skipped).\n- The fresh ordinary gate at 25653170 (tree 6852615d) passed: exit 0, 922.813 s wall, 1,954.899 s child CPU (one run). Node 57, Counting 55, plain 2,848 passed and 1 skipped, Native 795 passed and 2 skipped. No contradictory records and no unhandled errors.\n- After the gate only docs/kernel.md (identical to Main 994a638f), the note and the manifest change, so the documents-only rule applies.\n- The manifest (sha256 60e50c60) verifies against the sealed directory: 188 files, 0 bad, nothing writable, SHA256SUMS all OK. check-notes 994a638f..102169dd reports 0 warnings, and git diff --check is clean. The one seal change is the archive-driver.ts literal.\n- The note labels each figure by how it was taken: the old tail figures are the planner's earlier observations, the size bound is computed, the gate times are one run, and task.meta is absent and not reconstructed.\n\nArchitecture: sound for a temporary diagnostic. It adds no endpoint, read, admission, budget change or deployment. It rides on the existing archive-pass-diagnostic-v1 log line, which every default production pass emits, with a structural upper bound of 110,726 bytes for the capture field. Before relying on the hosted lines, the planner should confirm that one arrives whole in the Worker logs. The planner also owns removing the capture after the parent measurement.\n\nSecurity: no finding.\n- No body, signature, token, header, setting, SQL or path name can enter the record: inputs are copied field by field from closed lists, and non-numeric values make the record malformed instead of being kept.\n- Frames name public source files by index only.\n- The observer can slow the original clock, as the note states; it cannot grant work.\n\nSimplification: acceptable. PUBLIC_CODE_FILES is a 97-row literal list that must track renames, and an unknown file leaves attribution incomplete rather than wrong. That is acceptable for a diagnostic that is to be removed.\n\nVerdict: approved at exact head 102169dd. The builder lands. This landing closes child 7e4b543c only; parent 0f0eeab7 and every other BR-4 outcome under 15b0f8ab stay open. No builder deployment; the planner deploys dap-grow after landing and reads the rows.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:308fc21eb50af39ecd6a0a75b4c29a36c4011a47","binding":"assigned","head":"102169dd08a3a6f3b6228de24f9085c8369e75dd","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5c022e8bbfbf7eef402508915a01839850303e8b\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fe7fca472e0d652f5f4a0b0d98b6d33a79881985\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5c022e8bbfbf7eef402508915a01839850303e8b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}